                <pb facs="0706" n="638" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg638"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. Sanford to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 436.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1867-07-06"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            6, 1867.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> A report to the King from the minister of
                    the interior, under date of the 3d instant, appears in the Moniteur of this day,
                    proposing, in view of the cessation of the cattle plague in the states of the
                    Zollverein, and its amelioration in Holland, the removal of certain restrictions
                    upon various importations from those countries.</p>
                <p>A royal decree follows under date of 4th instant, removing the interdiction of
                    the entry and transit of horned cattle, hides, &amp;c, from the states of the
                    Zollverein, and of swine and pork, and dried hides from Holland.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. S. SANFORD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
